### Decomposition decisions

- **4 prompts instead of the spec's 5.** The suggested split made prompts 3 and 4 both edit the same `build` target, which cannot be independently verified and would force a non-functional placeholder recipe in between. I merged them into one coherent Makefile edit (prompt 3). This stays within the Sizing Guide for a major feature (3-4) and respects the anti-over-decomposition rule.
- **Prompt 1** lands `hack/build-cluster.sh` + `hack/cluster-alias.sh`; **prompt 2** lands `hack/build-job.yaml` + `hack/build-cluster-bootstrap.sh` + `hack/dockerconfig.json.tpl`. All five bodies were fetched over HTTPS from the exact pinned refs (`agent-task-executor@91a7e64e…`, `go-skeleton@eb050aa2…`) and verified byte-for-byte by extracting the fenced blocks and diffing against the fetched files (all MATCH).
- **Prompt 3** adds `BUILD_TARGET ?= local`, `BUILD_TIMEOUT ?= 3600`, `BUILD_REPO_URL ?= https://github.com/$(IMAGE).git`, `BUILD_PUSH_SECRET ?= buildkit-push`, wraps `build` in `ifeq ($(BUILD_TARGET),local)` with the local `docker build` line frozen verbatim, and puts the defaulted-`VERSION` guard inside the cluster branch only. I validated the proposed Makefile in a scratch directory: local `make -n build` emits the single unchanged docker line; cluster `make -n` emits `IMAGE='docker.io/bborbe/openldap'` / `DOCKER_REGISTRY='docker.io'` and `hack/build-cluster.sh`; the guard exits non-zero with `the cluster arm needs an explicit VERSION`; `precommit`/`test` pass.
- **Prompt 4** makes `upload`/`clean` echo `nothing to do` for non-local targets, adds `## Unreleased`, and runs a consolidated AC7 sweep.

### YAGNI / spec-constraint decisions (surfaced as reviewer comments in prompts)

- **No `BUILD_NAMESPACE` knob** — the Job manifest fixes `namespace: build`.
- **No `BUILD_DOCKERFILE` knob** — `hack/build-cluster.sh` already defaults `DOCKERFILE=Dockerfile`.
- **No `ALLOW_DEFAULT_VERSION` bypass** — spec Non-goal; guard is unconditional inside the cluster branch.
