No prompt's `<verification>` uses bare `git`, `docker`, `kubectl`, `dark-factory`, or `scripts/*`. All checks are `make -n`, `bash -n`, `grep`/`test`, the guard path (which exits before any cluster call), and the cluster-target echo paths. The repo uses `workflow: worktree` (`.git` masked), so no git-dependent checks were emitted. The operator rung (real Job, `crane digest`, node name) remains on the spec's Verification ladder, untouched.

